.TH MU2EDAQ\-BOOTSTRAP 1 "2026-04-21" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-bootstrap \- manage the mu2edaq\-main git submodule repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh
is a helper script for working with the
.B mu2edaq\-main
meta-repository, which aggregates the Mu2e DAQ software suite as a collection
of git submodules.
It wraps common submodule workflows into four simple commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clone
Clone
.B mu2edaq\-main
from GitHub together with all submodules in a single step.
Equivalent to:
.RS
.EX
git clone --recurse-submodules git@github.com:Mu2e/mu2edaq-main.git
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI update " [name]"
Fetch and merge the latest commits from the remote tracking branch of every
submodule, or of the single submodule identified by
.IR name .
After this command the working tree of each submodule reflects the current
state of its upstream
.B main
(or default) branch, but the parent repository's recorded pointers are not yet
updated \(em run
.B bump
to commit them.
.TP
.BI bump " [name]"
Stage the updated submodule pointer(s) in the parent repository and create a
commit recording the new HEAD(s).
If
.I name
is supplied only that submodule's pointer is staged; otherwise all changed
pointers are staged.
Prints a reminder to run
.B git push
afterwards.
.TP
.B status
Print a one-line summary for each submodule showing its local HEAD commit,
the corresponding remote HEAD, and whether it is up-to-date or behind/diverged.
.SH EXAMPLES
Clone the full suite onto a new machine:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh clone
.EE
Pull the latest code for all packages and record the update:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh update
    ./mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh bump
    git push
.EE
Update and bump a single submodule:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh update mu2edaq-controlcenter
    ./mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh bump  mu2edaq-controlcenter
    git push
.EE
Check which submodules are behind their remotes:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh status
.EE
